{
  "notes": "Techno, A phrygian, 128 BPM, straight. A one-finger minor chord stab (TRIO MIN STAB: every stab a minor triad, so the progressions use only the minor chords i, iv and vii) on the offbeats with a quarter-note dub echo, a rolling Casio bass that holds an A pedal in sixteenths around the kick (with the phrygian flat 2 at the end of the bar), the player's resonant pluck on the Smart Keys, and the TECHNO kit: four on the floor, clap on 2 and 4, open hats on the offbeats, rim syncopations, a ride in the lift. Scenes: A PLATFORM is the intro with kick and hats, no bass; B NIGHT LINE runs i for three bars and vii for one; C OVERPASS climbs iv vii with the bass following the roots; D UNDERPASS drops to iv i. ENERGY: stabs alone, then kick and bass, then the full kit in eighths, then sixteenths, fills and ratchets. All material is original.",
  "format": "flowstate-world/1",
  "id": "metro_beat",
  "name": "METRO BEAT",
  "category": "GROOVE",
  "blurb": "Techno on the night line",
  "tempo": {"bpm": 128, "min": 120, "max": 134},
  "key": {"root": "A", "scale": "PHRY"},
  "tracks": [
